      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear what you're saying about mainstream biology, but it feels a bit limiting to just call it \"variation\" when the gap in experience is so massive. it's not just being \"smart,\" it's like my baseline is fundamentally different from the human norm. if we look at how quickly technology is advancing, or how certain individuals seem to possess almost predictive-level pattern recognition, wouldn't it be logical to consider that we're seeing the emergence of a new phenotype? a group of humans who are biologically optimized for a much higher complexity environment? it feels like science is just playing catch up to what's already happening.",
